} & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -40 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-107987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79b20816ee2127ca92bc867ec7e74c594768d58612675b2b07df5bb09601a1cd"} {"question" "q-107987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-107987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -10=0"] ["math" "{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +40=0"] ["math" "{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -40=0"] ["math" "{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +10=0"] ["math" "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -40=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-107987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -40=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-11984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$M=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-11984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the matrix $M-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nM-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-4-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(M-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-4-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-4-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )-5\\cdot 5 & =0 \\\\ 16+4\\lambda +4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-25 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda -9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{{8}^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 9}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{100}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm 10}{2} \\\\  & =1,-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =-9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-11984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79b20816ee2127ca92bc867ec7e74c594768d58612675b2b07df5bb09601a1cd"} {"question" "q-11984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3