rmula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{{4}^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{64}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm 8}{2} \\\\  & =-6,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-12296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79b20816ee2127ca92bc867ec7e74c594768d58612675b2b07df5bb09601a1cd"} {"question" "q-12296" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-12296" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =-2$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =-4$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =2$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =2$  (double root)"] ["text" "There are no real eigenvalues"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-12296" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =2$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-5\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ -2+\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-3,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79b20816ee2127ca92bc867ec7e74c594768d58612675b2b07df5bb09601a1cd"} {"question" "q-9348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =-4$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =4$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)"] ["text" "There are no real eigenvalues"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the matrix $D-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿\n\n$$\nD-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(D-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ 9-3\\lambda -3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{(-6)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 5}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm 4}{2} \\\\  & =5,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79b20816ee2127ca92bc867ec7e74c594768d58612675b2b07df5bb09601a1cd"} {"question" "q-9347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =1$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =5$ (double root)"] ["text" "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =-1$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =1$"] ["text" "There are no real eigenvalues"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =1$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-7\\cdot 7 & =0 \\\\ 4-2\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-49 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -45 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 45}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{196}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 14}{2} \\\\  & =-5,9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-9340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/activity-met