1 \\\\ -3 & 8-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(8-\\lambda )-(-3)\\cdot 1 & =0 \\\\ 40-5\\lambda -8\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+3 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +43 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-13)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 43 \\\\  & =169-172 \\\\  & =-3 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-107852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79b20816ee2127ca92bc867ec7e74c594768d58612675b2b07df5bb09601a1cd"} {"question" "q-107852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-107852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =43$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =13$ (double root)"] ["text" "$\\lambda =13$ and $\\lambda =43$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =43$ (double root)"] ["text" "There are no real eigenvalues"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Develope