 :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79b20816ee2127ca92bc867ec7e74c594768d58612675b2b07df5bb09601a1cd"} {"question" "q-36778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-36778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\lambda =-2$  (double root)"] ["text" "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =-1$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =2$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =2$ (double root)"] ["text" "There are no real eigenvalues"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-36778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\lambda =-2$  (double root)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-36776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-36776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-6-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-6-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-6-\\lambda )(-10-\\lambda )-(-3)\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ 60+6\\lambda +10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+16\\lambda +66 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={16}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 66 \\\\  & =256-264 \\\\  & =-8 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions, and therefore, $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-36776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79b20816ee2127ca92bc867ec7e74c594768d58612675b2b07df5bb09601a1cd"} {"question" "q-36776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-36776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =-10$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =6$ and $\\lambda =10$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =8$ (double root)"] ["text" "$\\lambda =8$ and $\\lambda =5$"] ["text" "There are no real eigenvalues"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-36776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "There are no real eigenvalues"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-76364" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$N=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-76364" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the matrix $N-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nN-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(N-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda +\\sqrt{7}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =-\\sqrt{7}.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e5