cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-11983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -\\sqrt{3})(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-11983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79b20816ee2127ca92bc867ec7e74c594768d58612675b2b07df5bb09601a1cd"} {"question" "q-11983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-11983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =-\\sqrt{3}$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)"] ["text" "$\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\lambda =2$"] ["text" "There are no real eigenvalues"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-11983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\lambda =2$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-106995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-106995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =3.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-106995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/diffic