62/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79b20816ee2127ca92bc867ec7e74c594768d58612675b2b07df5bb09601a1cd"} {"question" "q-107843" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-107843" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =18$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =18$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =9$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =9$ (double root)"] ["text" "There are no real eigenvalues"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "q-107843" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =18$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c3c572d6561573158c4efb4ed120dac06fa1e72e365cf8c4e53797ddfb306c2"} {"question" "e-5479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/901d3a22065b48a8076b9c9aae5563c770c36c9ad40e4063c0f739847e1cda98.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/example-5479.json" "file_sha256" "b04c17da9272d16a946e8620dc244eac2a3dddff464169810feee5008c8bf3ff"} {"question" "e-5479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/0c6f9f860a1cf4d510f6c3d4d9c66b77496a354bb1e2cef1b69fd1178e4f15ab.png)\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4\\cdot 3 & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/example-5479.json" "file_sha256" "b04c17da9272d16a946e8620dc244eac2a3dddff464169810feee5008c8bf3ff"} {"question" "e-5481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/a1b88b7897649bb059cef39d40b2b052a13ac28282223b5688a1bce98296fb53.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/example-5481.json" "file_sha256" "93e90507bf982e7ad1eb0bd3620f5df99f12d08b9f3e4bfa719e1e362136465d"} {"question" "e-5481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/ca8f02e390e338b62956302ec45ea274ad73a51dafde3fe93b3d1e37dd663699.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}10-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-3\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ 70-7\\lambda -10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-17\\lambda +52 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{(-17)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 52}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm 9}{2} \\\\  & =13,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=13$ and $\\lambda=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/example-5481.json" "file_sha256" "93e90507bf982e7ad1eb0bd3620f5df99f12d08b9f3e4bfa719e1e362136465d"} {"question" "e-5480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/5ca3e07cfbe9e5d4956b1eab4393601f2a78b0b067d17312e71cbac993e28a86.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/example-5480.json" "file_sha256" "9a9e17e3a01be7181c4e9b80c1d23abddc1319d2c844832f19dcb8f9cce9a6fc"} {"question" "e-5480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/fdbcc62870aefab6214b2f24f53e9bc5654e5386639d4bc328dff3769aff2b45.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation. \n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/example-5480.json" "file_sha256" "9a9e17e3a01be7181c4e9b80c1d23abddc1319d2c844832f19dcb8f9cce9a6fc"} {"question" "e-5482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/603c59d43e3be000931e7279ac4d27be8aa92692f1528ec57ebd52172affa3cb.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/example-5482.json" "file_sha256" "817561094910241425810e41e7954976175c98c38d917bf1e8cf0029e394bb78"} {"question" "e-5482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/f91e4886c58db10f60fa666a870aed3c2f456b25e6afb560f857e9c36e81217c.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det (A - \\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )-9\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2\\sqrt{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the eigenvalues $\\lambda={\\color{red}3}$ and $\\lambda={\\color{blue}-2\\sqrt{3}}.$\n\nIf we look again at the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/aa89b93c6fabd2f3dc7063c85e253ded7482018a5f1c6dadedc74964194c5754.png)\nwe see that the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. This is true in general: the eigenvalues of a *triangular* or *diagonal* matrix are *always* given by the entries on the main diagonal!\n\n**Watch out!** For a general matrix (which is neither triangular nor diagonal), this might not be the case!" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/example-5482.json" "file_sha256" "817561094910241425810e41e7954976175c98c38d917bf1e8cf0029e394bb78"}] "usage" {"q-36776" [] "e-5480" [] "e-5482" [] "q-12296" [] "q-11983" [] "e-5481" [] "q-36758" [] "e-5479" []} "basis" 2336 "retractions" [[17592186092636 :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186092638 :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n\n$Q = \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186092462 :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186092021 :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186092021 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I$:\n﻿﻿﻿$\\begin{bmatrix}2 - λ & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}2 - λ & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(2 - λ)(2 - λ) - 4 \\cdot 3 &= 0 \\\\\n4 - 4λ + λ^{2} - 12 &= 0 \\\\\nλ^{2} - 4λ - 8 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186092023 :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186092023 :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I$:\n﻿﻿$\\begin{bmatrix}10 - λ & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7 - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}10 - λ & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(10 - λ)(7 - λ) - 3 \\cdot 6 &= 0 \\\\\n70 - 7λ - 10λ + λ^{2} - 18 &= 0 \\\\\nλ^{2} - 17λ + 52 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= (17 ± \\sqrt{(-17)^{2} - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 52})/(2 \\cdot 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{17 ± \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{17 ± 9}{2} \\\\\n&= 13, 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=13$ and $\\lambda=4$."] [17592186092022 :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186092022 :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 - λ & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(B - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}4 - λ & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(4 - λ)(4 - λ) - 0 \\cdot 0 &= 0 \\\\\n(λ - 4)^{2} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4$, which is a double root of the characteristic equation.\n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2$."] [17592186092024 :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186092024 :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I$:\n﻿﻿﻿$\\begin{bmatrix}3 - λ & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3} - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\det (A - \\lambda I) = 0\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}3 - λ & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3} - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(3 - λ)(-2\\sqrt{3} - λ) - 9 \\cdot 0 &= 0 \\\\\n(λ - 3)(λ + 2\\sqrt{3}) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the eigenvalues\n\n$$\n\\lambda={\\color{red}3}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\lambda={\\color{blue}-2\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nIf we look again at the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\nwe see that the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. This is true in general: the eigenvalues of a *triangular* or *diagonal* matrix are *always* given by the entries on the main diagonal!\n\n**Watch out!** For a general matrix (which is neither triangular nor diagonal), this might not be the case!"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186089209 17592186089210 17592186089211 17592186089212 17592186089213 17592186090282 17592186090283 17592186090284 17592186090285 17592186090286 17592186090294 17592186090295 17592186090296 17592186090297 17592186090298 17592186294526 17592186294527 17592186294528 17592186294529 17592186294530] "immutable_fields" [[17592186089208 :answer-field/correct] [17592186089208 :answer-field/id] [17592186089208 :answer-field/key] [17592186089208 :answer-field/type] [17592186090281 :answer-field/correct] [17592186090281 :answer-field/id] [17592186090281 :answer-field/key] [17592186090281 :answer-field/type] [17592186090293 :answer-field/correct] [17592186090293 :answer-field/id] [17592186090293 :answer-field/key] [17592186090293 :answer-field/type] [17592186294525 :answer-field/correct] [17592186294525 :answer-field/id] [17592186294525 :answer-field/key] [17592186294525 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
